## 2. Behaviour: `candidateCount` is the raw eligible-producer count

Range widens from `{0} ∪ [2,∞)` to `{0,1} ∪ [2,∞)` — 63 of 195 items.

**PASSING with the code present:** the three rows below all pass at HEAD.

**BREAK** — re-add the retired `< 2 ⇒ 0` gate at the `candidateCount` site
(`chain-builder-adapter.ts:341`):

```ts
-    candidateCount: producerRecipesFor(catalog, s.itemId, excludedMachineIds)
-      .length,
+    candidateCount: ((n: number): number => (n < 2 ? 0 : n))(
+      producerRecipesFor(catalog, s.itemId, excludedMachineIds).length,
+    ),
```

Compiles: `npx tsc -b` → exit 0.

**GENUINE FAIL** (full suite):

```
 FAIL  src/ui/chain-builder-adapter.test.ts > S21 P1 — producerRecipesFor is
       the comparison enumerator > counts a LONE eligible producer as 1 on a
       real preview row
 AssertionError: expected +0 to be 1 // Object.is equality

 FAIL  src/ui/chain-builder-adapter.test.ts > S20 P0 — candidateCount on
       preview rows > counts EVERY eligible producer per item (0, 1, or more)
       from the catalog
 AssertionError: expected +0 to be 1 // Object.is equality

 FAIL  src/ui/chain-builder-adapter.test.ts > S20 P1 — toProposalPreview
       candidateCount under exclusions > counts a LONE surviving producer as 1
       (S21 P1 — no ≥2 gate)
 AssertionError: expected +0 to be 1 // Object.is equality

 Tests  3 failed | 909 passed (912)
```

All three of the spec's count rows fire, on synthetic AND bundled fixtures.

**RESTORE + RE-RUN GREEN:** reverted; tree clean; suite green.

